78 cents. One fifth — F♯→C♯ — is narrowed by one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schisma (32805:32768), equal to 16384:10935 ≈ 699.977 cents. The remaining seven","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fifths are pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly because one syntonic comma times"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"one schisma equals one Pythagorean comma."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The four quarter-comma fifths make C–E a pure major third (5:4). Published in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"Die Kunst des reinen Satzes in der Musik","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", Part II."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Kirnberger III (Johann Philipp Kirnberger, 1779).","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/kirnbergerIII"},"references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning":{"abstract":[{"text":"Musical pitch, interval, and tuning system types.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","title":"IvorTuning"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament/kirnbergerIII":{"abstract":[{"text":"Kirnberger III (Johann Philipp Kirnberger, 1779).","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/kirnbergeriii","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kirnbergerIII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topi